preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: "MoE-Direct: Byte-preserving MoE expert streaming from NVMe on consumer hardware"
  authors:
    - name: "tmxkzm1925-max"
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21739367
  year: 2026
  notes: "Technical note describing the method and measurement protocol (Zenodo, defensive publication)"
abstract: >-
  MoE-Direct serves Mixture-of-Experts LLMs whose weights exceed system memory
  by keeping repacked, 4KiB-aligned expert records on NVMe and reading them on
  demand into a deterministic slot cache, with SHA-verified byte-equal expert
  records, token-ID parity verified under deterministic greedy OFF/ON
  protocols, asynchronous queue-depth I/O, optional next-layer expert prefetch
  on validated profiles, and a counterfactual replay methodology for
  validating expert prefetch before implementation. Measured on a 32GB RAM /
  16GB VRAM Windows PC: Qwen3.5-122B (72.3GiB GGUF) at 5.59-5.69 tok/s decode
  (official gated runs, 2.32-2.34x over the plain mmap arm); a 1T-class model
  (416.8GiB GGUF, Q3_K experts) produced coherent output at about 1 tok/s in
  non-gating runs.
